{
  "notes": [
    "Source-tagged ledger for the QRegExp -> QRegularExpression migration (spec 4.3).",
    "Every row records where the pattern lives (or why the row is a ledger pin without a live consumer yet), which engine and options the old code used, the exact migrated pattern and options, and the fixed expected matches/captures/replacement. No expected value is computed from the code under test.",
    "Rows whose production consumer is scheduled in a later task carry 'productionOwner'; they are fixed expectations the owner task must satisfy, not a test-only reimplementation of that owner's logic. Wildcard rows drive QRegularExpression::wildcardToRegularExpression itself, which is the API the owner uses.",
    "'oldOptions' documents the pre-migration behaviour that must be preserved; 'migration' records what the conversion changed. A row with 'expectInvalid' pins that a malformed built-in pattern is detected instead of silently matching everything."
  ],

  "rows": [
    {
      "id": "html-src-prefix-negated-schemes",
      "family": "HTML tags/resources",
      "source": "stardict.cc:468",
      "oldEngine": "QRegExp",
      "oldOptions": "Qt::CaseInsensitive, non-minimal",
      "pattern": "(<\\s*(?:img|script)\\s(?:[^>]*\\s)?src\\s*=)(?!\\s*[\"']?(?:data|https?|ftp):)(\\s*[\"']?)",
      "newOptions": ["CaseInsensitive"],
      "migration": "non-capturing tag group keeps capture order 1 = tag prefix, 2 = opening quote; the negative lookahead still admits a quote before the scheme check",
      "subject": "<img src=\"a.png\">",
      "expectedCaptures": [["<img src=\"", "<img src=", "\""]]
    },
    {
      "id": "html-src-prefix-rejects-data-uri",
      "family": "HTML tags/resources",
      "source": "stardict.cc:468",
